      "body_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Please explain why is the snapshot for <code class=\"notranslate\">DmaStreamInner</code> is justified:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Why is better than wrapper method using <code class=\"notranslate\">rwarc</code> locks?</li>\n<li>Who will provide the snapshot? Who tracks it? Who ensures that the snapshot is \"the\" current state of the dma stream?</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To me this looks unsound.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On a sidenote this design is intentional because tracking the runtime properties via <code class=\"notranslate\">RwArc</code> is not well-supported. Maintaining the invariant without reasoning about <em>how</em> invariant mutates provides little verification meanings</p>",
      "body_text": "Please explain why is the snapshot for DmaStreamInner is justified:\n\nWhy is better than wrapper method using rwarc locks?\nWho will provide the snapshot? Who tracks it? Who ensures that the snapshot is \"the\" current state of the dma stream?\n\nTo me this looks unsound.\n\nOn a sidenote this design is intentional because tracking the runtime properties via RwArc is not well-supported. Maintaining the invariant without reasoning about how invariant mutates provides little verification meanings",
      "body": "> Please explain why is the snapshot for `DmaStreamInner` is justified:\r\n> \r\n> * Why is better than wrapper method using `rwarc` locks?\r\n> * Who will provide the snapshot? Who tracks it? Who ensures that the snapshot is \"the\" current state of the dma stream?\r\n> \r\n> To me this looks unsound.\r\n\r\nOn a sidenote this design is intentional because tracking the runtime properties via `RwArc` is not well-supported. Maintaining the invariant without reasoning about *how* invariant mutates provides little verification meanings",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
